%% How a meal photo becomes a food-log entry
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as You (phone)
    participant FE as Snap meal page
    participant API as POST /api/food/analyze
    participant GEO as portions.py<br/>(container geometry)
    participant R as LLM router
    participant V as Vision model<br/>(Gemini / Groq / … / Ollama)
    participant DB as Nutrition lookup<br/>(library → USDA → OFF → web)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL

    U->>FE: Take photo (+ optional ingredients,<br/>container, fill level, known weight)
    FE->>FE: Compress to ≤1600 px JPEG
    FE->>API: multipart form
    API->>API: Auto-rotate, resize, save to /uploads/food
    API->>GEO: container volume × fill × density
    GEO-->>API: expected weight (e.g. 750 ml × 50% × 0.70 g/ml ≈ 262 g)
    API->>R: vision task + strict JSON prompt
    loop until one model succeeds
        R->>V: image + context
        alt 429 rate limit
            V-->>R: cooldown this model, try next
        else 401/403
            V-->>R: skip the whole provider
        else OK
            V-->>R: items, grams, ranges, hidden fats
        end
    end
    R-->>API: parsed JSON
    API->>API: Reconcile weights (known weight ▸ geometry ▸ vision)
    loop each item
        API->>DB: per-100 g values
        DB-->>API: verified values + source
        API->>API: blend DB + AI macros, low/high kcal range, confidence
    end
    API->>PG: food_analyses row (status, items, sources)
    API-->>FE: FoodAnalysis
    U->>FE: Review / edit items
    FE->>PG: POST /analyses/{id}/save → food_logs (+ tags, recompute day)
